from lib import *
C=9;S='maths'
lesson(C,S,'coordinate-geometry','distance-and-section-formula',"Distance, mid-point and section formula (Class 9)","Two houses on a grid","Two houses are at (2, 1) and (5, 5) on a town grid. A cable runs straight between them. How long is it, and where is its middle?",
["The distance between (x1, y1) and (x2, y2) is the square root of [(x2 - x1)^2 + (y2 - y1)^2]. @ distance formula",
 "It is Pythagoras theorem on the horizontal and vertical differences. @ Pythagoras",
 "The mid-point is ((x1 + x2)/2, (y1 + y2)/2). @ mid-point",
 "The point that divides the segment internally in the ratio m : n is ((m x2 + n x1)/(m + n), (m y2 + n y1)/(m + n)). @ section formula",
 "The points of trisection divide the segment in the ratio 1 : 2 and 2 : 1. @ trisection",
 "The centroid of a triangle is the average of its three vertices. @ centroid"],
("Find the distance between (2, 1) and (5, 5) and the mid-point.",[("Differences: 5 - 2 = 3 and 5 - 1 = 4.","Subtract each coordinate."),("Distance = square root of (9 + 16) = 5.","A 3-4-5 triangle."),("Mid-point = (3.5, 3).","Average each coordinate.")]),
("Write the distance formula and mid-point formula and explain where they come from.",["Pythagoras theorem","Mid-point is an average","Section formula uses the ratio m : n"],["Subtracting in the wrong order inside the square"]),
["Distance = root of sum of squared differences.","Mid-point = average of coordinates.","Section formula: ratio m : n.","Centroid = average of the three vertices."],
["n|Distance between (0, 0) and (6, 8) is|10|36 + 64 = 100.",
 "m|Mid-point of (2, 6) and (4, 10) is|(3, 8)|(6, 16)~That is the sum;(1, 2)~That is half the difference|Average of coordinates.",
 "t|Distance between two points cannot be negative.|True|It is a square root.",
 "n|Distance between (3, 4) and (3, 10) is|6|Same x, so just 10 - 4.",
 "t|The mid-point of (0,0) and (2,2) is (1,1).|True|Average each.",
 "n|y-coordinate of the mid-point of (1, 2) and (3, 8) is|5|(2 + 8)/2.",
 "n|Centroid x of (0,0), (6,0), (0,6) is|2|(0+6+0)/3.",
 "s|The point halfway along a line segment is its ____.|mid-point|Definition."])
lesson(C,S,'trigonometry','trigonometric-ratios-and-special-angles',"Trigonometric ratios and special angles (Class 9)","Climbing a ramp","A ramp rises 3 m over a horizontal length of 4 m. The ratio of rise to run tells us how steep it is - and the idea of a ratio of sides is the start of trigonometry.",
["In a right triangle, with respect to an angle A, the sides are opposite, adjacent and hypotenuse. @ opposite, adjacent, hypotenuse",
 "sin A = opposite / hypotenuse, cos A = adjacent / hypotenuse, tan A = opposite / adjacent. @ sin cos tan",
 "The ratios depend only on the angle, not on the size of the triangle. @ depend on the angle only",
 "Special angles: sin 30 = 1/2, cos 30 = root 3 / 2, tan 30 = 1/root 3; for 45 degrees sin = cos = 1/root 2 and tan = 1. @ special angles",
 "For 60 degrees: sin 60 = root 3 / 2, cos 60 = 1/2, tan 60 = root 3. @ 60 degrees",
 "Complementary angles: sin (90 - A) = cos A and cos (90 - A) = sin A. @ complementary",
 "sin squared A + cos squared A = 1. @ identity"],
("In a right triangle the legs are 3 and 4. Find sin A, cos A and tan A for the angle A opposite the side 3.",[("Hypotenuse = root(9 + 16) = 5.","Pythagoras."),("sin A = 3/5, cos A = 4/5.","Opposite 3, adjacent 4."),("tan A = 3/4.","Opposite over adjacent.")]),
("Define the three trigonometric ratios and list sin 30, sin 45, sin 60.",["Opposite, adjacent, hypotenuse ratios","1/2, 1/root 2, root 3/2","Complementary angle rule"],["Mixing up sin and cos"]),
["sin = opp/hyp, cos = adj/hyp, tan = opp/adj.","sin 30 = 1/2, sin 45 = 1/root 2, sin 60 = root 3 / 2.","sin (90 - A) = cos A.","sin^2 A + cos^2 A = 1."],
["n|sin 30 degrees =|0.5|1/2.",
 "t|tan 45 degrees = 1.|True|Opposite equals adjacent.",
 "m|cos 60 degrees equals|1/2|root 3 / 2~That is sin 60;1~That is cos 0|cos 60 = 1/2.",
 "n|If sin A = 3/5, hypotenuse 5 and opposite 3, the adjacent side is|4|9 + 16 = 25.",
 "t|sin A can be greater than 1 for an acute angle.|False|Opposite is shorter than the hypotenuse.",
 "n|tan 60 squared equals|3|tan 60 = root 3.",
 "t|sin 90 minus A equals cos A.|True|Complementary relation.",
 "s|sin A divided by cos A equals ____ A.|tan|Definition."])
lesson(C,S,'mensuration','herons-formula-and-solids',"Heron's formula, cuboid and cube","Painting a room","To buy paint you need the area of the walls; to fill a tank you need its volume. Heron's formula gives the area of a triangle from its three sides alone, and the cuboid and cube formulae give surface areas and volumes.",
["Heron's formula: area of a triangle with sides a, b, c is the square root of [s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)] where s = (a + b + c)/2. @ Heron's formula",
 "For a triangle with sides 13, 14, 15: s = 21, area = root(21 x 8 x 7 x 6) = 84 square units. @ 13, 14, 15",
 "Cuboid of length l, breadth b, height h: total surface area = 2(lb + bh + hl); lateral surface area = 2h(l + b); volume = l x b x h. @ cuboid",
 "Cube of side a: total surface area = 6 a squared, lateral = 4 a squared, volume = a cubed. @ cube",
 "The diagonal of a cuboid is root(l^2 + b^2 + h^2). @ diagonal",
 "Volume is in cubic units, area in square units; litres: 1000 cubic cm = 1 litre. @ units"],
("Find the area of a triangle with sides 7, 8 and 9 cm.",[("s = (7 + 8 + 9)/2 = 12.","Semi-perimeter."),("Area = root(12 x 5 x 4 x 3) = root 720.","s - a = 5, s - b = 4, s - c = 3."),("Area = 12 root 5, about 26.83 square cm.","720 = 144 x 5.")]),
("Write Heron's formula and the volume and surface-area formulae of a cuboid.",["s is half the perimeter","2(lb + bh + hl)","l x b x h"],["Using perimeter instead of semi-perimeter"]),
["Heron: area = root[s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)].","Cuboid: TSA 2(lb + bh + hl), V = lbh.","Cube: TSA 6a^2, V = a^3.","1000 cubic cm = 1 litre."],
["n|Semi-perimeter of a triangle with sides 6, 8, 10 is|12|24/2.",
 "n|Area of the triangle 3, 4, 5 by Heron (square units) is|6|s = 6, root(6 x 3 x 2 x 1) = 6.",
 "n|Volume of a cube of side 4 cm is|64|4^3.",
 "t|Surface area of a cube of side a is 6a^2.|True|Six equal faces.",
 "n|Volume of a cuboid 5 by 4 by 3 is|60|5 x 4 x 3.",
 "n|Total surface area of a cube of side 2 is|24|6 x 4.",
 "t|1 litre equals 1000 cubic cm.|True|Standard unit conversion.",
 "s|The area of a triangle from its three sides is given by ____ formula.|Heron's/Heron|Definition."])
lesson(C,S,'statistics','data-and-central-tendency',"Collecting data, mean, median and mode (Class 9)","Marks in a test","Ten pupils scored 6, 7, 7, 8, 9, 9, 9, 10, 4, 5 in a quiz. How do we describe the whole class with one number? The mean, median and mode each do it in their own way.",
["Statistics deals with collecting, organising and interpreting data. Raw data is arranged in a frequency table. @ frequency table",
 "The mean is the sum of all observations divided by their number: mean = sum of x / n. @ mean",
 "The median is the middle value after arranging in order; for an even number of values it is the average of the two middle ones. @ median",
 "The mode is the value that occurs most often. @ mode",
 "For the marks above the sum is 74 and n = 10, so the mean is 7.4; in order they are 4, 5, 6, 7, 7, 8, 9, 9, 9, 10 so the median is (7 + 8)/2 = 7.5; the mode is 9. @ 7.4, 7.5, 9",
 "For grouped data we use class marks (mid-points) with frequencies: mean = sum of f x / sum of f. @ grouped data",
 "Choose the mean for general use, the median when there are extreme values and the mode for the most popular item. @ which to use"],
("Find the mean, median and mode of 3, 5, 5, 6, 9.",[("Mean = (3 + 5 + 5 + 6 + 9)/5 = 28/5 = 5.6.","Sum divided by number."),("Median: already in order, the middle (third) value is 5.","Five values, so the middle is the 3rd."),("Mode = 5 because it occurs twice.","Most frequent.")]),
("Explain mean, median and mode and when each is best.",["Mean is the average","Median is the middle value","Mode is the most frequent"],["Forgetting to sort before finding the median"]),
["Mean = sum / number.","Median = middle value of the ordered data.","Mode = most frequent value.","Grouped data uses class marks."],
["n|Mean of 2, 4, 6 is|4|12/3.",
 "n|Median of 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 is|5|The middle value.",
 "n|Mode of 2, 3, 3, 4, 5, 3 is|3|It appears three times.",
 "t|The median must always be one of the data values.|False|For an even count it is the average of two middle values.",
 "n|Median of 2, 4, 6, 8 is|5|(4 + 6)/2.",
 "t|The mean is affected by extreme values more than the median.|True|One very large value shifts the mean.",
 "n|Mean of 10, 20, 30, 40 is|25|100/4.",
 "s|The most frequently occurring value is the ____.|mode|Definition."])
lesson(C,S,'probability','empirical-and-classical-probability',"Classical and empirical probability","Tossing a coin 100 times","Toss a coin 100 times and you may get 52 heads - close to half. Probability is about how likely things are, and it can be worked out in two ways: by reasoning and by experiment.",
["An experiment with several possible outcomes is a trial; the set of all outcomes is the sample space. @ sample space",
 "Classical probability: P(E) = number of favourable outcomes / total number of equally likely outcomes. @ classical",
 "Empirical probability: P(E) = number of times E occurred / total number of trials. @ empirical",
 "Probability is always between 0 and 1, with 0 for an impossible and 1 for a sure event. @ 0 to 1",
 "For one die, P(even) = 3/6 = 1/2 and P(prime) = 3/6 since 2, 3 and 5 are prime. @ die examples",
 "The more trials we perform, the closer the empirical probability comes to the classical probability. @ many trials",
 "A card drawn from 52: P(king) = 4/52 = 1/13. @ cards"],
("A bag has 3 red and 5 blue balls. One ball is drawn at random. Find P(red) and P(not red).",[("Total balls = 8; red balls = 3.","Count outcomes."),("P(red) = 3/8.","Favourable over total."),("P(not red) = 1 - 3/8 = 5/8.","Complement rule.")]),
("What is the difference between classical and empirical probability?",["Classical: equally likely outcomes","Empirical: from experiment","Both lie between 0 and 1"],["Thinking probability can exceed 1"]),
["P(E) = favourable / total.","Empirical = times E happened / trials.","0 <= P(E) <= 1.","P(not E) = 1 - P(E)."],
["n|A die is rolled. The number of outcomes is|6|1 to 6.",
 "m|P(head) for a fair coin is|1/2|1~That would be a sure event;2~A probability cannot exceed 1|One favourable of two.",
 "t|The probability of an impossible event is 0.|True|By definition.",
 "n|P(getting 7 on a normal die) is|0|There is no 7.",
 "n|A coin is tossed 50 times and shows heads 27 times. Empirical P(head) as a decimal is|0.54|27/50.",
 "t|P(E) + P(not E) = 1.|True|Complement rule.",
 "n|Bag with 2 red and 3 blue balls: P(blue) as a decimal is|0.6|3/5.",
 "s|Probability found by performing an experiment is ____ probability.|empirical|Definition."])
